&lt;h3 id=&#34;english--русский&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;[https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/blob/dev/README_RU.md]%28https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/tree/dev?tab=readme-ov-file#%29&#34; &gt;English&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/blob/dev/README_RU.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Русский&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://amnezia.org?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_website-readme-en&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Amnezia&lt;/a&gt; is an open-source VPN client, with a key feature that enables you to deploy your own VPN server on your server.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://amnezia.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/blob/dev/metadata/img-readme/uipic4.png&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Image&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;website--alt-website-link--documentation--troubleshooting&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://amnezia.org?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_website-readme-en&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Website&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://storage.googleapis.com/amnezia/amnezia.org?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_website-readme-en-mirror&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Alt website link&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.amnezia.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.amnezia.org/troubleshooting&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Troubleshooting&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!TIP]
If the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://amnezia.org?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_website-readme-en&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Amnezia website&lt;/a&gt; is blocked in your region, you can use an &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://storage.googleapis.com/amnezia/amnezia.org?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_website-readme-en-mirror&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Alternative website link&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://amnezia.org/en/downloads?utm_source=github&amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_button-readme-en&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/blob/dev/metadata/img-readme/download-website.svg&#34; width=&#34;150&#34; style=&#34;max-width: 100%; margin-right: 10px&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href=&#34;https://storage.googleapis.com/amnezia/amnezia.org?m-path=/en/downloads&amp;utm_source=github&amp;utm_campaign=amnezia_button-readme-en-mirrow&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/blob/dev/metadata/img-readme/download-alt.svg&#34; width=&#34;150&#34; style=&#34;max-width: 100%;&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/releases&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;All releases&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.testiny.io&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/blob/dev/metadata/img-readme/testiny.png&#34; height=&#34;28px&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;features&#34;&gt;Features
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very easy to use - enter your IP address, SSH login, password and Amnezia will automatically install VPN docker containers to your server and connect to the VPN.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Classic VPN-protocols: OpenVPN, WireGuard and IKEv2 protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protocols with traffic Masking (Obfuscation): OpenVPN over &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/cbeuw/Cloak&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Cloak&lt;/a&gt; plugin, Shadowsocks (OpenVPN over Shadowsocks), &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.amnezia.org/documentation/amnezia-wg/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;AmneziaWG&lt;/a&gt; and XRay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Split tunneling support - add any sites to the client to enable VPN only for them or add Apps (only for Android and Desktop).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Windows, MacOS, Linux, Android, iOS releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for AmneziaWG protocol configuration on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.keenetic.com/ua/air/kn-1611/en/6319-latest-development-release.html#UUID-186c4108-5afd-c10b-f38a-cdff6c17fab3_section-idm33192196168192-improved&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Keenetic beta firmware&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;links&#34;&gt;Links
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://amnezia.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://amnezia.org&lt;/a&gt; - Project website | &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://storage.googleapis.com/kldscp/amnezia.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Alternative link (mirror)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.amnezia.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://docs.amnezia.org&lt;/a&gt; - Documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.reddit.com/r/AmneziaVPN&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://www.reddit.com/r/AmneziaVPN&lt;/a&gt; - Reddit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn_en&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn_en&lt;/a&gt; - Telegram support channel (English)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn_ir&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn_ir&lt;/a&gt; - Telegram support channel (Farsi)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn_mm&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn_mm&lt;/a&gt; - Telegram support channel (Myanmar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://t.me/amnezia_vpn&lt;/a&gt; - Telegram support channel (Russian)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://vpnpay.io/en/amnezia-premium/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://vpnpay.io/en/amnezia-premium/&lt;/a&gt; - Amnezia Premium&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;tech&#34;&gt;Tech
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;AmneziaVPN uses several open-source projects to work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.openssl.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;OpenSSL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://openvpn.net/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;OpenVPN&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.qt.io/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Qt&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://libssh.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;LibSsh&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.wireguard.com/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;WireGuard&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://xtls.github.io/en/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Xray-core&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://conan.io/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Conan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and more&amp;hellip;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;help-us-with-translations&#34;&gt;Help us with translations
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Download the most actual translation files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Go to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/amnezia-vpn/amnezia-client/actions?query=is%3Asuccess&amp;#43;branch%3Adev&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&amp;ldquo;Actions&amp;rdquo; tab&lt;/a&gt;, click on the first line.
Then scroll down to the &amp;ldquo;Artifacts&amp;rdquo; section and download &amp;ldquo;AmneziaVPN_translations&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unzip this file.
Each *.ts file contains strings for one corresponding language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate or correct some strings in one or multiple *.ts files and commit them back to this repository into the &lt;code&gt;client/translations&lt;/code&gt; folder.
You can do it via a web-interface or any other method you&amp;rsquo;re familiar with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;checking-out-the-source-code&#34;&gt;Checking out the source code
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Make sure to pull all submodules after checking out the repo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;git submodule update --init --recursive
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;hacking-guide&#34;&gt;Hacking guide
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Want to contribute? Welcome!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;build-requirements&#34;&gt;Build requirements
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://cmake.org/download/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;CMake&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compiler and underlying build system, depending on the target:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Linux] Any of &lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;gcc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Apple] &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://developer.apple.com/xcode/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Xcode&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://developer.apple.com/xcode/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Xcode command line tools&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Windows] &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vs_community.exe&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Visual Studio 2022&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vs_buildtools.exe&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;VS 2022 Build Tools&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Android] &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;#installing-android-sdk&#34; &gt;&lt;code&gt;Android SDK&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://ninja-build.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Ninja&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.qt.io/download-open-source&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Qt 6.10+&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; with the following modules:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core module for targeting platform (Desktop/Android/iOS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qt 5 Compatibility module&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qt Remote Objects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://conan.io/downloads&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Conan&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; package manager
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On MacOS is enough just to use &lt;code&gt;homebrew&lt;/code&gt; or install it in &lt;code&gt;.venv&lt;/code&gt; in project root&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other systems must have it in &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(Optional) Installer dependencies:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Windows/Linux] &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.qt.io/download-open-source&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;Qt Installer Framework&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[Windows] &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/wixtoolset/wix/releases&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;code&gt;WIX toolset&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;building-the-project-using-scripts&#34;&gt;Building the project using scripts
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run scripts located in &lt;code&gt;deploy&lt;/code&gt; directory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basically, if dependencies are located in default installation paths, the scripts will find them automatically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If they differ, specify them using the following variables:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;QT_INSTALL_DIR&lt;/code&gt; - Qt root installation folder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;QT_ROOT_PATH&lt;/code&gt;   - Qt framework root directory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;QIF_ROOT_PATH&lt;/code&gt;  - Qt Installer Framework root path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;ANDROID_HOME&lt;/code&gt;   - Path to Android SDK root folder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and others. Check scripts for more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unix-like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;13
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;14
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Build executables for the host platform&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Or just&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Build executables and installers for the host platform&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.sh --installer all
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Build Android APK and AAB&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.sh -t android --aab
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Call for help&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.sh -h
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Windows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-batch&#34; data-lang=&#34;batch&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;: Build executables for Windows&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.bat
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;: Build executables with IFW installer for Windows&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.bat --installer ifw
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;: Build executables with IFW and WIX installer for Windows&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.bat --installer ifw --installer wix
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;: Or just&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;deploy/build.bat --installer all
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;developing-the-project-in-ides&#34;&gt;Developing the project in IDEs
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Basically, you can use any IDE that handles CMake and Qt kits properly to run configure and build steps, and to navigate through the code nicely. For example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Qt Creator&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Visual Studio Code&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;Qt Extension Pack&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and so on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To use &lt;code&gt;Xcode&lt;/code&gt;, you have to configure project first by using &lt;code&gt;cmake&lt;/code&gt;. The easiest way to do it is to use &lt;code&gt;Qt Creator&lt;/code&gt; for configuration. Then open &lt;code&gt;AmneziaVPN.xcodeproj&lt;/code&gt; file from the build folder by using &lt;code&gt;Xcode&lt;/code&gt;. Note that none of the files changed are saved - the files actually getting changed in build directory. Copy them manually if necessary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Android studio&lt;/code&gt; could be used in the same way - just configure the project by using &lt;code&gt;cmake&lt;/code&gt; manually or by using &lt;code&gt;Qt Creator&lt;/code&gt;. Open &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;build-dir&amp;gt;/client/android-build&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;Android studio&lt;/code&gt; then. Do not forget to copy the changes - everything you do is saved under the build directory actually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;installing-android-sdk&#34;&gt;Installing Android SDK
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Android SDK could be installed using the following methods:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;Qt Creator&lt;/code&gt;. Use &lt;code&gt;Preferences&lt;/code&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;code&gt;SDKs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;Android studio&lt;/code&gt;. By default it installs necessary &lt;code&gt;SDKs&lt;/code&gt; automatically during the installation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manually by using &lt;code&gt;sdk-manager&lt;/code&gt;. Check &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://developer.android.com/tools&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;this&lt;/a&gt; page for details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;license&#34;&gt;License
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This project is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE) and also includes third-party components distributed under their own terms (see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;donate&#34;&gt;Donate
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Patreon: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.patreon.com/amneziavpn&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://www.patreon.com/amneziavpn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
